-- title:
--   Regularity at a supersingular node gives membership in the local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q \ge 5$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $a \in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2} = a$ and lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no point $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$ other than $P = 0$. Let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$1 \cdot q$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$. Assume that $f$ and its image under the Fricke involution `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` both lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the modular ring over $A$ at the complement of the prime kernel of the reduction map. Assume further that for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring) which is centred at $(a, a^q)$ — meaning that for some $x, y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x = a$ and $\mathrm{red}\,y = a^q$ one has $W.\mathrm{ord}(j - x) > 0$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q - y) > 0$, where $j$ is the series `jq` and $j_q$ its $q$-fold $q$-expansion, both transported to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — one has $W.\mathrm{ord}(f) \ge 0$. Finally let $K \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ such that $a$ is the reduction of some element of $\mathrm{coeffSubring}\,A\,K = A \cap K$, and assume $f$ lies in `fieldOver (1 * q) K`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the constant series from $K$ together with the two series $j$ and $j_{1 \cdot q}$. Then $f$ lies in `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) (coeffSubring A K) (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`: there are two-variable polynomials $r, s$ over $A \cap K$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(a, a^q)$ after reduction and $f \cdot s(j, j_q) = r(j, j_q)$.
--
--   This is the regularity criterion for the local ring of the plane model of $X_0(q)$ over $A \cap K$ at the supersingular node $(a, a^q)$ of its characteristic-$q$ fibre: a modular function defined on both Fricke sides and with no pole at any place centred at the node already lies in that local ring. It is used in the construction of two-branch normalisations at nodes of $j$-invariant $0$ and $1728$ and in the prolongation-tuple analysis of place specialisations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_mem_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_isIntegral_of_mem_fieldOver_of_redRestrict_eq_of_forall_centred_ord_nonneg.lean

